WEBVTT

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:13.330
Mr. Ryoma, I'm sorry to call on you so suddenly.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:16.080
How is Bamboo Forest doing?

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.580
Yes, the two you introduced,
Ms. Carla and Mr. Callum,

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.080
are working very well.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.120
I've also hired a few other employees,
so the shop can run without me.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.950
I see, that is good to hear!

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:33.500
In fact, it's kind of going so well
that I'm getting a bit scared.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.950
I've asked you to come today
for yet another business opportunity.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.250
Oh?

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:44.160
You are currently delivering us a steady supply
of ingots and sticky slime strings.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:49.330
In addition to that, we wanted to ask you
to deliver us lots of waterproof fabric.

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:50.580
Lots?

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:55.660
Are you aware of the upcoming
grell frog outbreak season?

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:58.040
Yes, I heard about that.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:02.950
Their hide makes armor, and their organs
make good medicine and sell well.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:10.450
That's why many adventurers head out
to the lake during the outbreak season.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:17.040
Waterproof garments and waders
would be very popular for this.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.950
I see. I will start making them right away.

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:24.790
Thank you very much!

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:27.120
It's so great to work with you.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:04.000
"Episode 10"
"The New Slimes, with the Slimes"

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.580
What is that one eating?

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:11.700
It's iron powder.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:12.750
Iron?

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:18.000
I was thinking, perhaps by having it eat iron,
it would evolve into a metal slime.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.750
It's an experiment.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:27.120
I see. By the way, are you making
the waterproof fabrics at the mines?

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.290
Yes, that place is good to avoid interference.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:34.200
In that case, may I join you?

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.200
I don't mind, but why?

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.080
Violin practice?

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:47.580
Yes. I can practice to my heart's content here.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:52.950
I didn't know you had
that talent as well... But why?

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:58.290
I told you about the limour birds
coming to the lake.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:03.200
Playing music is essential to taming them.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.290
Music...

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:11.660
Limour birds communicate with and
identify each other using their beautiful songs.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:17.790
If they like the music, it makes it easier
for them to accept the taming contract.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.290
I see... I didn't know.

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:22.330
That's why I need to practice.

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:27.620
Please don't mind me, Mr. Ryoma.
You can work on your waterproof fabric.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.000
Oh, yes.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.000
Okay, let's go back to our own work now.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:24.160
Great work, Mr. Ryoma. And you, too, slimes.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:29.370
Same to you, my lady. It will take
a bit of time to dry the fabric,

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:30.910
so while we wait, as promised...

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:32.540
The dolls!

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:34.120
Y-Yes.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.660
Please make them!

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:40.500
Create Block.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.120
Break Rock.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.120
Playing Clay.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.910
Good, now on to the details...

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:01.700
It's done.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:07.950
This is wonderful! I'm a doll now!

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:10.830
Thank you so much, Mr. Ryoma!

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:13.250
I will treasure this!

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.120
Oh, this is me!

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:24.000
And this is me!

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:28.790
Also me, Sebas, Araune, Lilian...

00:06:28.790 --> 00:06:31.910
Exquisitely done.

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:35.040
Mr. Ryoma's craftsmanship
is impressive, as always.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.830
I'm glad you like it.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:41.620
Of course we do! Thank you so much!

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:45.160
I'm flattered to the point of feeling
a bit embarrassed, but I'm happy.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:50.580
Hey Elia, why don't you take this
with you when you go to school?

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:51.500
Huh?

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:55.790
Yes, good thinking.
It will keep you from being lonely.

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:58.080
Yes! I will do that!

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.040
Oh, Mr. Ryoma, please make a doll of yourself!

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:03.950
Huh? Of me?

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.580
Yes.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:08.620
I will take you with me!

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:12.370
Y-Yes!

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:18.200
The next day, I checked in with the shop.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:23.000
Next customer!

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.580
Over here please!

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.160
Please.

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:28.160
Thank you, come again!

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:30.870
Number 8 is ready.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:35.160
Since everything was going fine,
I went to the mines.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.950
Now all I have to do is wait for it to dry.

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:48.540
I can't leave here though... What to do...

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:50.700
Oh, I know!

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:55.950
I haven't done combat training
with the slimes for a while. Let's do that!

00:07:55.950 --> 00:08:00.660
Good, everyone! Keep at it!

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:06.250
I'll go one-on-one with
the king scavenger slime!

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:07.500
Let's go!

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:15.750
Immune to physical attacks, as I thought.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:25.790
Good! Stay on the move, and keep attacking!

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:32.660
Yes! Hold the enemy down like that!

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:47.580
That was a good workout. Is the fabric ready?

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:48.580
Hm?

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:52.830
What's wrong?

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:57.790
Evolution?!

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:03.080
It worked!

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:10.000
So heavy... It seems different
from the metal slime, though...

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:14.200
Monster Appraisal...

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:17.410
Iron slime?

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:23.500
Iron... I guess it's because of
all the iron it ate...

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:27.000
But I thought the metal slimes ate iron, too...?

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:29.910
Appraisal...

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:35.040
Metal included, iron oxide, aluminum oxide.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:36.750
I get it!

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:39.830
If you eat lots of different metals,
you become a metal slime,

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:44.080
and if you eat just pure iron,
you become an iron slime.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.910
Now I know how you evolve!

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:54.750
Good work, everyone.

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:57.790
Oh, Manager. Hello.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:09:59.830
Hello, Ms. Fina.

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:05.700
It's great how the cleaner slimes
work so hard without complaining.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:08.000
We should follow their example.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:11.750
You work very well, too, Ms. Fina.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.370
What's wrong?

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:18.080
They split up?!

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:21.950
Yes, now the cleaning work
will be even more efficient.

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:24.660
Really?! That's great!

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:27.580
Well, it's not me who's doing great
in this case, it's the slime.

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:32.370
What's going on, everyone?

00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:34.080
Oh, Manager.

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:36.000
About our sales today...

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:37.790
Did we incur losses or something?

00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:41.290
Oh no, we had a profit, but...

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:45.700
Three times more than yesterday?!

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:49.000
How did it grow so quickly?!

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.080
We had many huge contracts this morning.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.290
Word got around about our service.

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:59.120
Representatives from the blacksmiths,
carpenters, and iron foundry came in.

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:02.540
They were all very happy
with how clean things got!

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:04.660
We're also seeing many more
individual customers, too!

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:06.080
Business is booming!

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:09.500
I see... I didn't think it would get this big...

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:11.620
I'm truly surprised!

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:18.080
It's all thanks to all of you.
Thank you so much for working so hard.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:24.370
Mr. Ryoma, this is the least we could do,
as hired employees.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:26.950
I'm glad you feel that way.

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:31.700
But please don't hesitate to
let me know if you have any issues.

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:33.700
Issues...?

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:35.620
Can't think of any.

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:39.580
This is such a comfortable workplace,
there's no issue at all.

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:42.830
Anyone who complains about
working here would be wrong!

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:44.660
Well good...

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:51.040
I forgot about holidays!
It's such a basic necessity!

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:55.620
I've come from the bureau of labor standards.

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:59.620
One of your employees has filed a complaint.

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:02.370
Exploitative workplace, no good!

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:08.250
What's wrong, Manager?
You look pale all of a sudden.

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:13.750
I'm sorry, I totally forgot about your holidays.

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:15.000
Holiday?

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:15.950
Huh?

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:21.040
Manager, are you saying that we're all
going to get scheduled days off?!

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:23.250
I-Isn't it obvious?

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:27.120
Let's see... We can close
the shop one day a week,

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:29.450
or we can take holidays in shifts...

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:30.950
I'm so glad...!

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:32.700
Is this a dream?!

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:34.450
You're overreacting.

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:41.700
Manager, it is not common for a non-local
laborer to have set vacation days.

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:43.250
Really?

00:12:43.250 --> 00:12:47.950
Our families apologized to us
when we left our town!

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:51.750
They were so sorry they had to
force us to work in the city!

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:58.500
If we got hired by the wrong employer,
we could get overworked with little pay,

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:01.870
or worse, put our chastity at risk.

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:04.790
That definitely was a worry!

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:08.580
It is unfortunately true that there are
some employers who do those things.

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:12.450
It is a thing to watch out for as an employee.

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:17.000
So sexual harassment and
employee exploitation exist in any world...

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:22.120
The goal of this shop is to run a clean business
and treat its employees well.

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:23.540
Thank you for your cooperation!

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:26.160
Yes! Thank you!

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:29.580
Everyone, dinner is ready.

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:30.950
Yes, I was waiting!

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:32.790
So hungry!

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:35.540
Manager, please stay and eat if you can.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:37.330
Thank you!

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:42.250
The oil won't come off at all.

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:45.200
Look how lively this one is.

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:48.040
--Looks delicious!
--It's staring right at us!

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:50.950
Hello, Ms. Maylene.

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:54.540
Hello, Ryoma, doing guild work today?

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:58.000
Yes, my employees can
run the shop all by themselves now.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:02.200
That's quite a step up,
owning your own business and hiring people.

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:03.950
I was just lucky.

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:07.910
Really? I don't think luck alone
could take you that far.

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:10.370
It's all about real skills.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:14.790
I see... Well, I'll go see
if there are any good jobs.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.290
Oh, Ryoma.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:17.250
Yes?

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:20.540
It's not a job, but I have
something nice for you.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:21.870
Something nice?

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:27.370
There's an adventuring party from
out of town called Pier of Sikum.

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:29.080
Pier of Sikum?

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:32.950
They said they caught a rare breed of slime.

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:35.950
Details! Please!

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:42.250
They tried to sell it to the Tamer's Guild,
but they got refused.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:45.290
Slimes are quite neglected.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:48.750
So are you saying that slime is up for sale?

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:50.410
What do you think? You want it?

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:53.040
I do! Very much!

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:55.410
Do you know where they are right now?

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:59.950
This is where the Pier of Sikum are...?

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:02.120
This isn't abandoned, is it...?

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:18.450
Hello, are you the Pier of Sikum?

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:20.790
Yes, and you are?

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:26.540
I'm sorry I didn't introduce myself.
I am Ryoma Takebayashi, adventurer and tamer.

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:28.750
Really, at your age?

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:33.080
Hah! A kid like you, adventurer?!

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:34.750
Stop it, Sein.

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:38.950
Sorry, he's in a bad mood right now.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:44.580
I heard the story. You couldn't
sell your rare slime...

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:47.500
Yeah, and he's not taking it well.

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:52.160
Are you mocking us?!

00:15:56.910 --> 00:16:01.830
That's right, we're idiots!

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:06.790
We heard that even slimes
can sell well if it's a rare breed.

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:11.910
So we came all the way
out to this town, yet... nothing...

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:18.370
It's important to drink in moderation...

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:26.410
Hey, don't throw up here!

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:29.660
I'm sorry about all of that.

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:34.290
Let's start over. I am Shin,
leader of the Pier of Sikum.

00:16:34.290 --> 00:16:35.660
And I'm Kai.

00:16:35.660 --> 00:16:38.160
So what is your business with us?

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:42.700
I'd like to purchase the rare slime
that you couldn't sell.

00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:44.410
That slime?

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:45.750
But why?

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:53.830
I collect and study slimes. If it really is
a rare breed, I would love to get it.

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:57.910
I see... Well, it would be
great for us if you could buy it.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.370
How much are you charging?

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:03.370
Could you set the price?

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:07.580
The Tamer's Guild told us it's worthless,
so it's hard for us to come up with a price.

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:11.200
In that case, may I see the slime?

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:14.580
I will pay extra if it's a type of
slime I don't yet own.

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:15.580
That would do.

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:16.870
Wait there.

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:20.580
In here...

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:22.120
Be careful.

00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:24.160
Excuse me.

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:26.290
What kind of slime could it be...?

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:36.910
This is... some kind of fluid?
I've never seen this before.

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:40.500
What do you think?

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:44.540
I will pay extra for this!

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:46.500
R-Really!

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:47.950
Great!

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:49.790
So...

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:51.750
How about this?

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:53.080
Seriously?!

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:56.870
H-Hey, we're glad to see that, but are you sure?

00:17:56.870 --> 00:18:03.500
Yes, it's thanks to you that I am able to
get my hands on a new breed of slime.

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:07.910
I see. Well, we have no problem with that.

00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:11.330
I will take this then. Thank you very much!

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:13.660
We should be thanking you.

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:17.500
Now we don't have to worry about
cash for the immediate future.

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:19.580
It should calm Sein down.

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:23.540
I know how not having money
could be unsettling...

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:27.910
I know! If you want to make some money,

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:31.750
you might want to stay in this town for a while.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:37.910
Every year, there's an outbreak
of grell frogs in a nearby lake.

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:39.580
Grell frogs...

00:18:39.580 --> 00:18:44.410
Yes, they sell well as armor material
and medicinal ingredients.

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:46.660
You can check with the guild.

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:50.330
Really? That's... That's very helpful.

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:53.000
We'd like to repay you in some way, but...

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:55.500
That's not necessary, but...

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:59.660
If you could, please visit
my shop as a customer.

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:00.660
Shop?

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:04.580
I run a laundry service as a side business.

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:07.410
Wow, that's impressive.

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:13.250
It's called Bamboo Forest. We can clean
goblin grime, too. Please pay us a visit.

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:16.620
We definitely will.

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:18.450
Thank you!

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:26.410
Okay.

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:31.250
Let's execute the taming contract.

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:45.700
Good, contract complete!
Now, let's do the appraisal...

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:50.750
Bloody slime. It fits the
appearance perfectly, I guess.

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:55.500
It has a "vampirism" skill,
so I'm sure it must feed on blood...

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:06.290
It's drinking!

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:14.620
It went inside?! Is it sucking all of
the blood from the blood vessels?

00:20:14.620 --> 00:20:17.080
I didn't know such a slime existed...

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:28.330
I guess the blood is all let out now.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:32.750
Isn't this extremely useful for
eating beasts and monsters?

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:34.580
There must be many uses.

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:40.370
Good to meet you, bloody slime.

00:21:02.330 --> 00:21:05.620
Ryoma really likes slimes.

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:10.790
The slimes must be happy, too,
to be treated so well.

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:14.660
Yes, his facial expression is
so much brighter now.

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:18.120
He looks every bit like a normal kid.

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:23.500
Yes, it wasn't a mistake
to bring him to this world.

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:25.290
I'm glad.

00:21:25.290 --> 00:21:29.870
Oh, it's so easy to get sentimental
at my advanced age.

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:40.080
The grell frog outbreak was approaching.

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:42.290
Mr. Ryoma.

00:21:42.290 --> 00:21:47.620
My father, mother, and grandfather
are teaching me taming magic tomorrow.

00:21:47.620 --> 00:21:49.330
Would you like to join us?

00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:50.790
Taming magic?

00:21:50.790 --> 00:21:54.080
Yes, I think there would be a lot to learn.

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:59.040
Of course! I would love to
see you use taming magic.

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:00.830
I'm glad.

00:22:00.830 --> 00:22:02.870
Let's leave together then.

00:22:02.870 --> 00:22:08.580
Yes. I can't wait to see what kind of
taming magic you can show me.

00:22:08.580 --> 00:22:11.160
Oh, you're so eager.
